   All Prop 1(a)/Lemma S/Lemma O/halving/landing/partition checks passed: True; table mismatches against shells.out: 0
   Note on "visits": inside S_j = (2^D y_j, 2^(D+1) y_j] a halving leaves the shell (y/2 <= 2^D y_j) and two odd steps leave it
   ((3/2)^2 > 2), so any two indices of the orbit in S_j are automatically separated by an odd letter and a maximal run in S_j has
   at most 2 indices (THM-4506 Prop. C(a)). Hence m(j) = number of qualifying INDICES; the script's "shell runs" both undercount
   (a run holding 2 dippers) and overcount (window visits to S_j cut off by an earlier drop are not dippers of j).
   Regularity form: N(X) = #E + #Dip + #ND with #E <= k (0 for an infinite orbit). Averaged form => N(X) <= C L^mu N(X2^-D) + #ND + C L^2 + k;
   the note's "+1" (an extra N(X 2^-D)) and the absorbed k only weaken it. Converse: #Dip = N(X) - #ND - #E <= (C L^mu + 1) N(X2^-D) + C L^2,
   i.e. the averaged form with C -> C + 1. Both directions hold up to constants; the note's "both directions are the definitions" is right.
   Ratio definition: the script's N(X)/N(X 2^-D) restricts BOTH counts to indices with a full window (i <= M-k); the unrestricted ratio
   differs (e.g. 1.32 vs 1.39, 1.76 vs 1.91 on the record orbit at L = 24, 32). For the record orbit at L = 48, 64 every value is below
   X 2^-D (max 2^38.8 < 2^42), so ratio = 1.00 is vacuous there, not evidence of regularity.
