3. Gilbreath's difference triangle
   (a) rule algebra, new[i] = |row[i] - row[i+1]|:
       |a-b| = 2*(a/2 XOR b/2) on {0,2}: True; |1-a| = 1 for a in {0,2}: True
       defect d >= 4 at p with 0/2 neighbours: new[p-1] = d - row[p-1] (left neighbour) in all 20000 trials: True;
       ALSO new[p] = d - row[p+1] (a stationary copy, right neighbour) in all trials: True; two rows later cell p-1 is back in {0,2}: 20000/20000.
       So "moves one cell to the left per row, shrinks by 2 when the cell to its left is 2" is exact for the leftmost FRONT only;
       the seed also leaves a stationary copy that can re-emit fronts (a light cone with left speed 1 and right speed 0).
