          stationary copy adds a few per cent (j >= 3) through re-emitted fronts. The threshold j/F -> 0 and the exponential-in-F decay are right.
          Meeting a 2 always shrinks the front by exactly 2 while its left neighbour is in {0,2}; the leftmost defect never meets a 4 on its left
          (everything left of the frontier is 0/2 by definition), so the "4 or larger" case only concerns collisions between two defects.
